WoW64 AOT code caches linked into an image: run them in place (FEX 3bec2ac, on top of 0009)

Port of patches/fex/0005 to Madeira's FEX fork, for the WoW64 module on iOS.

WinPad's tools/cache2macho turns each AOT code cache into an object whose
linker resolves every reference from the code to the data area;
tools/cache2macho/aotindex.py adds an index of them (_fexaot_index). On
iOS the objects are linked into the app, so the code arrives in its signed
text segment and FEX must neither copy nor write it.

- CodeCache::LoadLinkedCache takes an image's _meta (the cache file without
  its code, behind an "FXAM" header), _text (the code) and _data (a
  writable data area). It fills the data area like LoadCache, but uses the
  code where the image put it: every page counts as loaded and the code is
  ReadOnlyCode. LoadCache's header parsing, data area fill and relocation
  grouping move into helpers shared by both.
- The image's data area is ordinary memory, not the RX view of the JIT
  pool, so its link records carry DATA_ONLY_LINK_RECORD_LINKED and
  ExitFunctionLink and the delinker store to them directly instead of
  through DualMap::WriteAddr.
- xtajit is a Windows DLL and cannot dlsym, so the host loads the image and
  puts the address of its index in WINE_IOS_AOT_INDEX.
  ImageTracker::LoadImageCache looks the image's file id up there first and
  falls back to the cache file.

